    exampleHands: [
      'Opening deal: 2-4 player(s), 3 card(s) per player, 1 deck(s), initial visibility face_down.',
      'Opening flow: start in play; each_player_clockwise may use play_card before round end.',
      'Scoring check: Standard Scopa points (scopa/sweep, most cards, most coins/diamonds, settebello, primiera) plus Scalette: Scaletta bassa (A-2-3 coins) = 3 points, extend upward to Horse/Queen for up to 9; Scaletta alta (K-Q-J coins) = 5 points, extend downward to 2 for up to 11; Scala (all coins/diamonds) wins the game outright. Target typically 11 or more (21, 31, 41 when using extra Scalette points). Expected outcome: First player or team to reach the agreed target (usually 11 or more) wins. Ties broken by an extra hand. Taking all coins/diamonds (Scala) wins immediately..',
